
================ Baseline ================
$ docker compose ps --format table {{.Service}}\t{{.Status}}
SERVICE   STATUS
api       Up 2 seconds (health: starting)
db        Up 59 seconds (healthy)
$ curl -s -w  HTTP %{http_code}\n localhost:8000/ready
{"status":"ready","db":"up"} HTTP 200

================ Inject failure: stop the database ================
$ docker compose stop db
 Container apex-ops-api-db-1 Stopping 
 Container apex-ops-api-db-1 Stopped 

================ Symptoms ================
$ curl -s -w  HTTP %{http_code}\n localhost:8000/health
{"status":"ok"} HTTP 200
$ curl -s -w  HTTP %{http_code}\n localhost:8000/ready
{"status":"not ready","db":"down"} HTTP 503
$ curl -s -w  HTTP %{http_code}\n localhost:8000/items
{"detail":"database unavailable"} HTTP 503

================ Investigate ================
$ docker compose ps -a --format table {{.Service}}\t{{.Status}}
SERVICE   STATUS
api       Up 11 seconds (healthy)
db        Exited (0) 8 seconds ago
$ docker compose logs --tail=4 api
{"timestamp": "2026-10-28 22:34:13,820", "level": "WARNING", "logger": "apex", "message": "readiness check failed", "error": "(psycopg.OperationalError) failed to resolve host 'db': [Errno -2] Name or service not known\n(Background on this error at: https://sqlalche.me/e/21/e3q8)"}
{"timestamp": "2026-10-28 22:34:13,820", "level": "INFO", "logger": "apex", "message": "request", "request_id": "f4d07d3277c94b138395f27250680238", "method": "GET", "path": "/ready", "status": 503, "duration_ms": 3972.33}
{"timestamp": "2026-10-28 22:34:17,704", "level": "ERROR", "logger": "apex", "message": "database error", "path": "/items", "error": "(psycopg.OperationalError) failed to resolve host 'db': [Errno -2] Name or service not known\n(Background on this error at: https://sqlalche.me/e/21/e3q8)"}
{"timestamp": "2026-10-28 22:34:17,704", "level": "INFO", "logger": "apex", "message": "request", "request_id": "8b58407ccefc46f089f04288975c0da7", "method": "GET", "path": "/items", "status": 503, "duration_ms": 3844.4}

================ Fix: start the database and verify recovery ================
$ docker compose start db
 Container apex-ops-api-db-1 Starting 
 Container apex-ops-api-db-1 Started 
[2026-10-28T22:34:18Z] service ready again
$ curl -s -w  HTTP %{http_code}\n localhost:8000/ready
{"status":"ready","db":"up"} HTTP 200
$ curl -s localhost:8000/items
